# tvm-recover — local configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (same directory) and fill in what applies to this machine:
#
#     cp .env.example .env          # PowerShell: Copy-Item .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is git-ignored, so your paths never get committed. NOTHING here is required: every setting
# also has a command-line flag, and blank means "use the built-in default". This file exists so the
# defaults for *this* machine live in one place instead of in shell exports or in the source.
#
# Precedence:  command-line flag  >  existing environment variable  >  `.env`  >  built-in default
#
# Syntax: `KEY=VALUE`, one per line. Blank lines and `#` comments are skipped. A leading `export `
# is allowed and ignored. Matching quotes around a value are stripped. A leading `~` expands to your
# home directory. `$VAR` is NOT expanded — a Windows path may legitimately contain `$`.
# Set a key to empty to disable it; to use a value containing spaces, leave it unquoted.


# =============================================================================================
# 1. Targets — what to analyse
# =============================================================================================

# TVM_MODULE — the protected module (engine side).
# Used by: probe.ir_acceptance, probe.loopcorpus, probe.loopfire, probe.readfallback,
#          probe.block_exits, probe.entry_shapes, and any probe run without a positional argument.
# Must be the build you actually measured: a same-named file from another protector build yields
# one block and `unreadable`, which reads like engine failure and is a wrong path.
# TVM_MODULE=C:\Program Files\AntiCheatExpert\SGuard\x64\SGuardSvc64.exe
TVM_MODULE=

# TVM_SAMPLES — root of a sample corpus.
# Used by: llvm/kernel_corpus.py, llvm/freeze.py, llvm/entry_denominator.py, tests.
# This is the directory that CONTAINS `07-samples/extended/` — the tools append that suffix.
# TVM_SAMPLES=C:\Users\me\ACE\handoff\tvm-devirt-evidence-20261012
TVM_SAMPLES=

# TVM_HOST — the host PE to patch (write-devirt tests only).
# Falls back to TVM_SAMPLES/SGuardSvc64.exe, then main/samples/SGuardSvc64.exe; when none exist the
# 5 host-patching tests SKIP and the other 49 still run.
# TVM_HOST=C:\Program Files\AntiCheatExpert\SGuard\x64\SGuardSvc64.exe
TVM_HOST=

# TVM_HOST_DIR — the directory a `probe.scan_tvm0` sample sweep should walk.
# Used by: probe.scan_tvm0 examples and session scripts; not a required input.
# TVM_HOST_DIR=C:\Program Files\AntiCheatExpert\SGuard\x64
TVM_HOST_DIR=


# =============================================================================================
# 2. Directories — where input and output go
# =============================================================================================

# TVM_LISTINGS — the listing corpus the backend consumes by default.
# Blank -> out/hard-cases-listings-final (seeded from fixtures/listings-final on checkout).
# TVM_LISTINGS=out\hard-cases-listings-final
TVM_LISTINGS=

# TVM_OUT — root for every tool's output. Blank -> out/
# TVM_OUT=out
TVM_OUT=

# TVM_REFERENCE — the output oracle (tvm-devirt.exe). Not shipped: it is a comparison oracle only,
# and reading its source would turn a recovery into a transcription. When unset, the checks that
# need it report `unavailable` rather than 0/0 success.
# TVM_REFERENCE=refs\tvm-devirt-mirror\tvm-devirt.exe
TVM_REFERENCE=


# =============================================================================================
# 3. Recovery budgets — the numbers every other number depends on
# =============================================================================================
# These are engine defaults, not preferences. `tests/test_budget_defaults.py` fails if
# devirt.DEFAULT_STEPS and explore.DEFAULT_STEP_BUDGET drift apart. Changing them changes every
# figure in every report: quote the budget with the number, or `probe.measure_diff` refills it.

# TVM_STEPS — steps per block before a block is TRUNCATED. Blank -> 900000
# At 400000 the root 0x140169e9d truncated a block; at 900000 it settles 17 blocks / 0 unresolved.
TVM_STEPS=

# TVM_BLOCKS — block budget per root. Blank -> 512
TVM_BLOCKS=

# TVM_HANDLERS — handler-derivation sample size. Blank -> 900
TVM_HANDLERS=


# =============================================================================================
# 4. Backend — the IR -> LLVM IR -> PE path
# =============================================================================================
# Needs llvmlite==0.50.0 and, on Windows, MSVC link.exe/cl.exe on PATH. No system LLVM.

# TVM_PAYLOAD_OPT — codegen level, one of 0 1 2 3. Blank -> 0 (chosen for readability).
# Checked, not trusted: the differential runs at every level you ask for.
TVM_PAYLOAD_OPT=

# TVM_PAYLOAD_MEM — guest-memory mode for the payload. Blank -> sealed
#   sealed  : route guest accesses through the sealed byte map (required for a real process;
#             without it the code addresses the analysis addresses, which mean nothing elsewhere)
#   absolute: leave the analysis addresses in place (diagnostic only)
TVM_PAYLOAD_MEM=

# TVM_PAYLOAD_SPLIT — split threshold for large functions. Blank -> 1000
TVM_PAYLOAD_SPLIT=

# TVM_PAYLOAD_FUEL — loop fuel budget written into the payload. Blank -> no explicit fuel
TVM_PAYLOAD_FUEL=


# =============================================================================================
# 5. Toolchain
# =============================================================================================

# GHIDRA_HOME — Ghidra install dir (frontier/readability measurements only).
# Unset -> `analyzeHeadless.bat` is searched on PATH; if neither, the measurement reports Ghidra
# unavailable instead of producing an empty table.
# GHIDRA_HOME=C:\tools\ghidra_12.1.3_PUBLIC
GHIDRA_HOME=

# MSVC link.exe / cl.exe: put their directory on PATH, or set TVM_MSVC_BIN and the payload builder
# uses the executables there instead. This is the setting most likely to differ between machines.
# TVM_MSVC_BIN=C:\Program Files\Microsoft Visual Studio\2022\Community\VC\Tools\MSVC\14.44.35207\bin\Hostx64\x64
TVM_MSVC_BIN=


# =============================================================================================
# Notes
# =============================================================================================
# - Output goes under `TVM_OUT` (default `out/`, git-ignored). The fixed-point listing corpora ship
#   under `fixtures/` and are seeded into `out/`, so the backend runs before you have a module.
#   Delete `out/` and restore from `fixtures/listings/`, `listings-branch/`, `listings-final/`.
# - `z3-solver` is optional: without it path conditioning stays and only the bounded dispatch proof
#   is skipped. `probe.z3_boundary` measures that boundary rather than asserting it.
# - A missing corpus or module never becomes a silent zero: the tool prints what it needs and exits
#   2, or the test skips.
